# Helium Rapid DSL (ANTLR4) Extension

This workspace builds the Helium Rapid DSL tooling used in Cursor:
- `helium-dsl-language-server/` - language server
- `helium-rapid-dsl-mcp/` - MCP server
- `helium-vscode-tooling/` - build, packaging, validation pipeline
- `helium-dsl-vscode/` - extension client

## Primary target

- Primary IDE target is Cursor.
- Use `cursor --install-extension ...`, not `code --install-extension ...`.

## Debug workflow expectation

When debugging extension/LSP/MCP/VSIX issues, run needed build/package/install steps directly instead of asking the user to do them, unless blocked by missing credentials/secrets.

## Project diagnostics config

Helium Rapid projects use `helium-rapid-dsl-project.json` at the DSL root. Besides debug settings, `diagnostics.unused` includes **`languageEntries`** (default **Info**): unused keys in `.lang` files vs references in `.mez` / `.vxml`. Set to `"None"` for noisy legacy `en.lang` files. **`models`** (default **Info**) reports persistent object types with no type references in indexed `.mez`; set `"None"` to disable.
